<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ghurak</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 737 or 738</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ghurak was the ikhshid, or king, of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarkand">Samarkand</a> in the early 8th century. He came to power around 710, shortly before the Umayyad general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qutayba-ibn-muslim">Qutayba ibn Muslim</a> took the city in 712, and then ruled as a tributary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphate</a>. He kept up relations with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang China</a> and the Turgesh, shifting sides between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabs">Arabs</a> and the Turks to preserve his rule.</p></div>
